agic day in march last year  at just after 1 40 in the afternoon on  the 15th of march last year  emergency services received the first  calls  a shooting was underway during friday  prayers at the al-noor mosque in central  christchurch  i saw one gun in the floor  and police was stopping here there was a  lot of people died  injured in total 44 worshipers were  killed by brenton tarrant at el nor  in an attack he live streamed on the  internet he then moved on to his second  target across town  the linwood mosque where he killed a  further seven people  the youngest victim just three years old  the eldest  77. he was arrested by police as he was  making his way to a third mosque in a  town nearby  it is clear that this can now only be  described  as a terrorist attack that was  determined because of the pre-planned  nature of the attack  and the ideology tarrant subscribed to  the australian had studied the layout of  the mosques  and their busiest times he'd uploaded a  manifesto detailing his white supremacy  beliefs  and his hatred of muslims and  non-european immigrants  as the wider population rallied around  the new zealand muslim community  attention turned to the high-powered  weapons he fired  how he obtained them and in some cases  modified them legally  i can tell you one thing right now our  gun laws  will change less than a month later most  semi-automatic weapons became illegal  and a government buyback scheme for guns  began  in march this year tarrant surprised  prosecutors by entering a guilty plea  that meant there'd be no trial but the  judge wanted some of the 40 survivors  and family members of those killed  to have the opportunity to speak  directly to the gunman in court  more than 60 statements were given  during the sentencing  he had no issue with linda armstrong  he didn't even know her  instead filled with his own racist  agenda  this coward hid behind his  big powerful guns and shot little old  linda from afar  she never even stood a c